 "model": "small.en",
 "text": "Australia was already racing to push a military road through that gap, the road that became the Stuart Highway, to move troops north. So a Japanese force in Darwin could bomb, block, and threaten. But marching south? Close to impossible. Tokyo's generals could see the trap. An army stuck in the north, facing Australian and American counterattacks, with supply lines stretching thousands of kilometers back to Japan. Exactly the kind of endless war they were already stuck in in China.",
